# Branch naming (mandatory)

Every implementation change happens on `feature/<feature_name>`.

- `feature_name` is kebab-case only: `capstone-design-pack`, `langfuse-setup`, `extractor-thin-slice`
- No extra slashes in `feature_name` (`feature/foo/bar` is forbidden)
- Never `feat/`, `fix/`, `chore/`, or a bare ticket id
- Never commit on `main` or `master`. Create or switch to `feature/<feature_name>` first
- One feature per branch. New work = new `feature/` branch from updated main

```
# Wrong
git checkout main && git commit
git checkout -b feat/extractor
git checkout -b feature/extractor/thin-slice

# Right
git checkout -b feature/extractor-thin-slice
```

# Push before switching (mandatory)

**Never leave a branch until its work is committed and pushed.** Work that exists only locally is invisible to the author, cannot be reviewed, and is lost if the workspace is reset.

Before `git checkout` / `git switch` to a different branch:

1. `git status` is clean — nothing uncommitted, nothing stashed and forgotten
2. Commit with a real message (what changed and why)
3. `git push -u origin feature/<feature_name>` — confirm it succeeded, do not assume
4. Open the PR, or say plainly that it is unpushed and why

A failed push is a **blocker, not a footnote**. Report it and stop; do not switch away and carry on.

## Stacked branches

When splitting accumulated work, later branches usually contain earlier ones. Target each PR at the branch below it, not at `main` — otherwise every PR shows the whole pile and none of them are reviewable.

```
# Right — each PR shows only its own delta
feature/a  -> main
feature/b  -> feature/a
feature/c  -> feature/b
```

Merge bottom-up. Push every branch in the stack; a stack with an unpushed link is broken.

## Auth check

This repo has more than one GitHub account in the local keychain. Only the repo owner can push or open PRs.

```
gh api user --jq '.login'   # must be the account with push access
gh auth switch --hostname github.com --user <owner>
```

A `403` on push or `must be a collaborator` on PR create means the wrong account is active — fix the account, do not work around it.
